-- SKAI-1954 (DB-01), batch 3 of the actor columns (models RosterBatch..WhatsAppUsageEntry): every column that names
-- a user (created_by_id, approved_by_id, owner_id...) now references that user pinned to the row's own school:
-- (school_id, <col>) -> users(school_id, id). A row can no longer name a missing user or another school's user.
--
-- Optional columns: ON DELETE SET NULL (<col>) clears only the actor and keeps school_id and the history row.
-- Prisma's schema cannot spell the column list, but its drift check reads both as SET NULL, so the schema says
-- onDelete: SetNull. tests/db/user-actor-keys.database.test.ts checks the column list is really there.
-- Required columns: ON DELETE NO ACTION, so a user with that history cannot be hard-deleted on its own. The app
-- never deletes users; they go with their school, which cascades these rows in the same statement.
-- users(school_id, id) is unique since batch 1 (20261124040000).
--
-- Keys are added NOT VALID and then validated. Indexes are plain CREATE INDEX (tables are small); for a large
-- production table build the index first with CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY under the same name.
-- Rollback: DROP CONSTRAINT "<table>_school_id_<col>_fkey" and DROP INDEX "<table>_school_id_<col>_idx" for the
-- names below.
SET lock_timeout = '10s';

